SWAT+ 62.0.1 bug fix, not part of the exchange mode: wallo_withdraw.f90 reads a place
of use's duty as pou(ipou)%pod(ipod)%duty, where ipou is the place's position in its
point of diversion's list and ipod the point of diversion's number. The right entry is
pou(pou_num)%pod(pod_num)%duty, which the routine computes a few lines later. Without
this, a place of use on any point of diversion but the first reads past the end of its
own list (0 or a stray value), and places of use sharing a point of diversion each
withdraw another's demand. docs/upstream-issue-wallo-withdraw.md; tests/test_allocation.py.

diff --git a/src/wallo_withdraw.f90 b/src/wallo_withdraw.f90
--- a/src/wallo_withdraw.f90
+++ b/src/wallo_withdraw.f90
@@ -25,20 +25,22 @@
       !! POD (source) object number from POD object
       j = pod(ipod)%typ_num
       
+      !! POD number from delivery object, pou number from loop in wallo_control
+      !! (swatplus-bmi: computed before the duty, which is indexed by them; ipou is the place
+      !! of use's position in the POD's list, not its number)
+      pod_num = pod(ipod)%pou(ipou)%pod_num
+      pou_num = pod(ipod)%pou(ipou)%num
+      
       !! set the duty or compensation for the POD - if compensation, then duty is umet duty for the POU
       if (wallo_comp == "y") then
-        wdraw_max = pou(ipou)%pod(ipod)%duty - poud_met(ipou)%pod(ipod)%deliv
+        wdraw_max = pou(pou_num)%pod(pod_num)%duty - poud_met(pou_num)%pod(pod_num)%deliv
       else
-        wdraw_max = pou(ipou)%pod(ipod)%duty
+        wdraw_max = pou(pou_num)%pod(pod_num)%duty
       end if
       
       !! zero out the withdrawal for the POD
       outflo_om = hz
       
-      !! POD number from delivery object, pou number from loop in wallo_control
-      pod_num = pod(ipod)%pou(ipou)%pod_num
-      pou_num = pod(ipod)%pou(ipou)%num
-      
       !! check minimum storage/flow limits and withdraw water from each POD
       select case (pod(ipod)%typ)
       
